---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { AUTHOR } from "@/consts";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How russrimmerman.com handles theme preferences, newsletter sign-ups, comments, and external services."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1
        class="text-ink-900 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl dark:text-white"
      >
        Privacy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400 mt-3 text-sm">
        Last updated July 30, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        This is a personal blog and portfolio. It does not currently include
        first-party advertising or analytics.
      </p>

      <h2>Theme preference</h2>
      <p>
        If you change the color theme, the site stores that preference in your
        browser's local storage. The value is used only to restore your selected
        light or dark theme on later visits.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter sign-up</h2>
      <p>
        When newsletter sign-up is available and you submit the form, your email
        address is sent to this site's managed API and then to the configured
        newsletter provider. The form also includes an empty anti-spam field. Do
        not submit the form if you do not want your address processed for the
        subscription.
      </p>

      <h2>Comments</h2>
      <p>
        Comments use Giscus and GitHub Discussions. The site does not connect to
        those services until you select <strong>Load comments</strong>. Their
        handling of account and request data is governed by their own privacy
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Azure Static Web Apps. Hosting services may
        process standard request data needed to serve and secure the site. Links
        to other websites take you to services with their own privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this site's privacy practices, email <a
          href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
